MoBetta: x87sidecar: Bridge x87 runs in blocks with all-zero flag liveness.

v2 bridging (flag-dead ALU in a gap) refused any block whose flag_liveness
bytes are all zero, in case the Rosetta build never fills the field. WoW
3.3.5a's segment-vs-box test (0x7f9480, the hottest x87 block at the
Dalaran fountain, 9.1% of exec-weighted x87 emit) is such a block: it
falls through into a loop header whose first flag op is `test`, so every
flag it writes is dead and every byte is 0. Its six `sub r32,r32` gaps
split it, and only 4 of its 13 x87 ops were joined.

Measured on Rosetta (macOS 27.2), x86_64 and i386 under Wine: the byte is
exact across a direct fall-through successor. A jc, sbb, mov;jz, a whole
x87 block then jc, or inc;jc there gives the sub 0x20/0x40; test or
mov;test gives 0 (an all-zero block). Exits the analysis cannot follow are
seeded 0xfe: indirect jmp, call, ret, a block cut at its length limit
(2036 instructions), and a fall-through across a page boundary. So
all-zero means every written flag is dead.

The guard now trusts an all-zero block once any block of the process has
had a nonzero byte (a per-process latch, x87bridge::flag_liveness_trusted);
blocks before the first one keep the per-block rule. The trust model is
the one v2 already used: a zero on the last writer before a fall-through
in a block with some nonzero byte also rested on the cross-block analysis.
X87_BRIDGE_ZERO_FL=0 restores the per-block rule. profile_analyze follows
it in its production config and fragmentation section (MB_ZERO_FL=0).

Tests: tests/test_bridge_fallthrough.c (in the suite and the
allocation-failure phase): ten live cases with a setter that leaves the
flag opposite to the sub's result before the region, so a bridged sub
gives a wrong value, and four dead cases that must join (X87_LOG_BRIDGE).
With flags_dead() forced true, all ten live cases fail; with the patch all
pass and the four dead cases join. Suite 1468 passed, 0 failed, 2 known
stock divergences. MoBetta tests/x87_bridge_stack.c under Wine:
bit-identical to stock, segbox loop ~512 -> ~339 ms (X87_BRIDGE_ZERO_FL=0:
~511). Session #28 Dalaran profile: 21.55 -> 20.05 ARM per x87 op,
0x7f9480 75.1G -> 24.1G exec-weighted ARM. In game at the Dalaran
fountain: 40-55 FPS with spikes into the 60s, vs 45-50 on 0002.

